{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ALNCD44csEGgABdmRySNVY","type":"tool_result","content":"# The criteria tables\n\nEach standard the report answers gets one table, supplied as a CSV file\nin the data directory: wcag.csv, section508.csv and en301549.csv. Which of\nthem you supply is decided by the report's edition\n([report details](report.md)): wcag.csv always, section508.csv for the\nsection508 and international editions, and en301549.csv for the en301549\nand international editions.\n\nEvery table has the same three columns, and the first line of the file\nnames them:\n\n```csv\ncriterion,conformance,remarks\n1.1.1,Partially Supports,\"Product images have text alternatives. The chart on the dashboard has none, so its figures are not available to screen reader users.\"\n1.2.1,Not Applicable,The product has no audio-only or video-only content.\n2.1.1,Supports,Every function can be operated from a keyboard.\n```\n\n- **criterion** is the criterion's number, exactly as its standard\n  numbers it: `1.1.1` for WCAG 2.2, `302.1` for the Revised Section 508\n  Standards, and `4.2.1` for EN 301 549. Validation refuses a number the\n  standard does not have. The package's references list every number each\n  table takes, with what the criterion asks: references/wcag-2.2.md,\n  references/section-508.md and references/en-301-549.md.\n- **conformance** is how far the product meets the criterion: one of\n  `Supports`, `Partially Supports`, `Does Not Support`, `Not Applicable`\n  and `Not Evaluated`, written exactly so. [What the levels\n  mean](conformance.md) says which to choose.\n- **remarks** says what the evaluation found. For Supports, say how the\n  product meets the criterion; for Partially Supports and Does Not\n  Support, say which functions fail and how; for Not Applicable, say why\n  the criterion does not concern the product. A field holding a comma, a\n  quote or a line break is written between double quotes, with each quote\n  inside it doubled (`\"\"`); a line break starts a new paragraph of the\n  remarks. Leave the field empty only when there is nothing to say.\n\nA row speaks for the whole product. Where its parts meet a criterion\ndifferently, such as its web pages, its documents and its software, give\nthe level the product as a whole earns and say in the remarks how each\npart fares.\n\n## Which criteria to list\n\nList each criterion of the table once, in the standard's order, which is\nthe order of its reference file. A complete report lists every criterion\nof the table, so that a reader can tell a criterion met from one left\nout: write Not Applicable for a criterion that does not concern the\nproduct, and Not Evaluated for one nobody evaluated. The rows appear in\nthe report in the order the file gives them.\n\nThe **WCAG 2.2** table lists the success criteria at Levels A and AA, and\nthose at Level AAA the vendor chose to evaluate. The report gives each\ncriterion's level beside its name. It also answers the parts of the other\ntwo standards that apply WCAG to web pages, documents and software, so\nthose standards' tables leave them out.\n\nThe **Revised Section 508** table lists the criteria of chapters 3 to 6:\nthe functional performance criteria (302), hardware (402 to 415), software\n(502 to 504) and support documentation and services (602 and 603). For\nsoftware, chapter 4's hardware criteria are Not Applicable.\n\nThe **EN 301 549** table, for EN 301 549 V4.1.1 (2026-09), lists the\nclauses outside clauses 9, 10 and 11.1 to 11.4, which the WCAG table\nanswers: the functional performance statements (4.2), the generic\nrequirements, authoring tools among them (5), real-time voice, text and\nvideo communication (6), video playback (7), hardware (8), software's\ninteroperability with assistive technology and its accessibility\nsettings (11.5 to 11.7), information and documentation about the product\nand its services (12), and relay services (13).\n-----\n# Conformance levels\n\nEvery row of a table gives the product one of five conformance levels for\nits criterion. Choose the level the evidence supports, and say what the\nevidence is in the row's remarks.\n\n- **Supports**: the product meets the criterion, and no defect against it\n  is known. A product that meets it through an equivalent alternative, such\n  as a second way of doing the same task that does meet it, supports it,\n  and the remarks name the alternative.\n- **Partially Supports**: the product meets the criterion in some of its\n  functions and not in others. The remarks name the functions that do not.\n- **Does Not Support**: the product does not meet the criterion in most of\n  its functions. The remarks say what fails.\n- **Not Applicable**: the criterion does not concern this product, such as\n  a captions criterion for a product with no video. The remarks say why.\n- **Not Evaluated**: the product was not evaluated against the criterion.\n  Use it for a Level AAA criterion the vendor chose not to evaluate, and\n  for nothing that a buyer's standard requires: a report that leaves a\n  required criterion unevaluated does not show conformance with it.\n\nWhen in doubt between two levels, choose the lower, and explain in the\nremarks. A buyer relies on a report as a statement of fact about the\nproduct.\n-----\n/report\tobject\trequired\tadditionalProperties=false\tReport details\n/report/date\tstring\trequired\tformat=\"date\"\tReport date\n/report/edition\tstring\toptional\tdefault=\"wcag\" enum=[\"wcag\",\"section508\",\"en301549\",\"international\"]\tEdition\n/report/methods\tstring\trequired\tmaxLength=8000 minLength=1 pattern=\"^[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u0008\\\\u000B-\\\\u001F\\\\u007F]+$\"\tEvaluation methods\n/report/notes\tstring\toptional\tmaxLength=8000 minLength=1 pattern=\"^[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u0008\\\\u000B-\\\\u001F\\\\u007F]+$\"\tNotes\n/report/product\tobject\trequired\tadditionalProperties=false\tProduct\n/report/product/description\tstring\toptional\tmaxLength=2000 minLength=1 pattern=\"^[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u0008\\\\u000B-\\\\u001F\\\\u007F]+$\"\tProduct description\n/report/product/name\tstring\trequired\tmaxLength=200 minLength=1 pattern=\"^[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u001F\\\\u007F]+$\"\tProduct name\n/report/product/version\tstring\toptional\tmaxLength=100 minLength=1 pattern=\"^[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u001F\\\\u007F]+$\"\tProduct version\n/report/vendor\tobject\trequired\tadditionalProperties=false\tVendor\n/report/vendor/contact\tstring\toptional\tmaxLength=200 minLength=1 pattern=\"^[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u001F\\\\u007F]+$\"\tContact\n/report/vendor/email\tstring\toptional\tformat=\"email\" maxLength=254\tContact email\n/report/vendor/name\tstring\trequired\tmaxLength=200 minLength=1 pattern=\"^[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u001F\\\\u007F]+$\"\tVendor name\n/report/vendor/website\tstring\toptional\tformat=\"uri\" maxLength=2048 pattern=\"^https?://[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u0020\\\\u007F]+$\"\tWebsite\n\nNext:\n  metais schema <package> report  — Prints the whole schema, with each field's description.\n  metais validate <package> --data <dir>  — Validates the inputs you gathered in a data directory against this schema.\n/wcag\tarray\trequired\tmaxItems=86 minItems=1\tWCAG 2.2 table\n/wcag/*\tobject\toptional\tadditionalProperties=false\tCriterion row\n/wcag/*/conformance\tstring\trequired\tenum=[\"Supports\",\"Partially Supports\",\"Does Not Support\",\"Not Applicable\",\"Not Evaluated\"]\tConformance level\n/wcag/*/criterion\tstring\trequired\tenum=[\"1.1.1\",\"1.2.1\",\"1.2.2\",\"1.2.3\",\"1.2.4\",\"1.2.5\",\"1.2.6\",\"1.2.7\",\"1.2.8\",\"1.2.9\",\"1.3.1\",\"1.3.2\",\"1.3.3\",\"1.3.4\",\"1.3.5\",\"1.3.6\",\"1.4.1\",\"1.4.2\",\"1.4.3\",\"1.4.4\",\"1.4.5\",\"1.4.6\",\"1.4.7\",\"1.4.8\",\"1.4.9\",\"1.4.10\",\"1.4.11\",\"1.4.12\",\"1.4.13\",\"2.1.1\",\"2.1.2\",\"2.1.3\",\"2.1.4\",\"2.2.1\",\"2.2.2\",\"2.2.3\",\"2.2.4\",\"2.2.5\",\"2.2.6\",\"2.3.1\",\"2.3.2\",\"2.3.3\",\"2.4.1\",\"2.4.2\",\"2.4.3\",\"2.4.4\",\"2.4.5\",\"2.4.6\",\"2.4.7\",\"2.4.8\",\"2.4.9\",\"2.4.10\",\"2.4.11\",\"2.4.12\",\"2.4.13\",\"2.5.1\",\"2.5.2\",\"2.5.3\",\"2.5.4\",\"2.5.5\",\"2.5.6\",\"2.5.7\",\"2.5.8\",\"3.1.1\",\"3.1.2\",\"3.1.3\",\"3.1.4\",\"3.1.5\",\"3.1.6\",\"3.2.1\",\"3.2.2\",\"3.2.3\",\"3.2.4\",\"3.2.5\",\"3.2.6\",\"3.3.1\",\"3.3.2\",\"3.3.3\",\"3.3.4\",\"3.3.5\",\"3.3.6\",\"3.3.7\",\"3.3.8\",\"3.3.9\",\"4.1.2\",\"4.1.3\"]\tCriterion\n/wcag/*/remarks\tstring\toptional\tmaxLength=4000 minLength=1 pattern=\"^[^\\\\u0000-\\\\u0008\\\\u000B-\\\\u001F\\\\u007F]+$\"\tRemarks\n\nNext:\n  metais schema <package> wcag  — Prints the whole schema, with each field's description.\n  metais validate <package> --data <dir>  — Validates the inputs you gathered in a data directory against this schema.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6768f6e0-85fd-4c76-8134-5b4dbe9da1bd","uuid":"cfe2b2d4-7f26-4e33-8451-0b572fb29593","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:32:09.207Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# The criteria tables\n\nEach standard the report answers gets one table, supplied as a CSV file\nin the data directory: wcag.csv, section508.csv and en301549.csv. Which of\nthem you supply is decided by the report's edition\n([report details](report.md)): wcag.csv always, section508.csv for the\nsection508 and international editions, and en301549.csv for the en301549\nand international editions.\n\nEvery table has the same three columns, and the first line of the file\nnames them:\n\n```csv\ncriterion,conformance,remarks\n1.1.1,Partially Supports,\"Product images have text alternatives. The chart on the dashboard has none, so its figures are not available to screen reader users.\"\n1.2.1,Not Applicable,The product has no audio-only or video-only content.\n2.1.1,Supports,Every function can be operated from a keyboard.\n```\n\n- **criterion** is the criterion's number, exactly as its standard\n  numbers it: `1.1.1` for WCAG 2.2, `302.1` for the Revised Section 508\n  Standards, and `4.2.1` for EN 301 549. Validation refuses a number the\n  standard does not